patent_rationale:
The eight retrieved records already cover the core design space:
- monolithic 2T current-matched architectures (P1, P6);
- three-terminal configurations (P6);
- solution deposition and planarization on textured silicon (P2, P7);
- hole-transport stack engineering from an industrial filer (P3);
- 4-terminal and overlay module integration and encapsulation (P4, P8).

Six of the eight records were published from 2022 onward, which signals a rapidly filling field, so the score is adjusted defensively from a moderate baseline. Preliminary gaps visible within this small sample include lead-free top cells on textured wafers, lifecycle and recycling, in-line metrology, and 2T module interconnection (P5, P2, P7, P4, P8). These are snippet-level landscape observations only. They are not freedom-to-operate conclusions, and claims-level review by qualified patent counsel is required. Large silicon incumbents active in tandems per market sources do not appear in this registry, so the true density is likely understated.

market_rationale:
Commercial demand is real but nascent. Two named companies have paid deployments: Oxford PV for utility-scale (M7, M2) and Trina for premium residential and distributed PV (M1). Oxford PV has delivered to module partners (M5). Several further actors show market formation:
- LONGi and JinkoSolar report record cells and pilot roadmaps (M2, M4);
- CubicPV is investing in U.S. pilot manufacturing (M4);
- the Noak spin-off has €5M in funding, and Hanwha targets end-2028 mass production, though these appear only as headlines (M1).

Third-party market-size estimates exist (M3, M6, M8). The score sits just below the active-market tier for three reasons. Revenue is small and undisclosed, the customers are unnamed, and the forecasts diverge roughly 12× for 2026 while covering broader perovskite rather than tandem-only revenue (M3, M6, M8).
